{"family": "ema_vfi", "task": "interpolation", "name": "EMA-VFI", "plain": "EMA-VFI (Zhang et al., CVPR 2023; large and small, for the middle frame or any time): makes the frame between two video frames from motion and appearance features that inter-frame attention extracts together, for slow motion and higher frame rates. Apache-2.0 code and weights.", "summary": "EMA-VFI (Zhang et al., CVPR 2023): video frame interpolation with inter-frame attention. A hybrid CNN and Transformer backbone; in its two window-attention stages (1/16 and 1/32 of the image) each frame attends to the other, and the attention map gives both the appearance features and motion features (the attention-weighted pixel offsets). Two heads estimate the flow to both frames and a fusion mask, a U-Net refines the blend of both warped frames. `ema-vfi` and `ema-vfi-small` are trained for the middle frame, `ema-vfi-t` and `ema-vfi-small-t` for any time in [0, 1].", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/MCG-NJU/EMA-VFI", "upstream_commit": "75b6f6a889e695df875e103374040d47a4cfac7c", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "Extracting Motion and Appearance via Inter-Frame Attention for Efficient Video Frame Interpolation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.00440", "date": "2023-03-01", "venue": "CVPR 2023", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["cudnn_hacc", "ema_warp"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "cuda_graphs", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "speed"}, {"name": "tta", "default": false, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "frame", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["CUDA graph replay keeps a private pool and static outputs for the current shape. Use `cuda_graphs=false` to disable